## 💻 Code

### Installation

1. Open `src/heater_control.ino` in Arduino IDE
2. Select Board: Arduino Uno
3. Upload to ATmega328P

### Core Logic

```cpp
// Constants
const int TEMP_PIN = A0;    // PT100 input
const int LEVEL_PIN = 2;    // Level sensor
const int SSR_PIN = 11;     // SSR control (Pin 17)
const int SETPOINT = 565;   // 60°C target
const int HYSTERESIS = 15;  // ±3°C deadband

// Control Logic
if (waterOk && adcValue < SETPOINT - HYSTERESIS) {
    digitalWrite(SSR_PIN, HIGH);  // Heat ON
} else if (adcValue > SETPOINT + HYSTERESIS) {
    digitalWrite(SSR_PIN, LOW);   // Heat OFF
} // else maintain state (hysteresis)
```

### Temperature Reference

| Temp | PT100 (Ω) | ADC Value |
|------|-----------|-----------|
| 20°C | 107.8 | 530 |
| 60°C | 123.2 | 565 |
| 100°C | 138.5 | 593 |

