## 🧪 Testing

### Proteus Simulation

1. Open `hardware/schematics/heater_control.dsn`
2. Set ATmega clock: 16MHz
3. Upload .hex file
4. Run simulation (F12)
5. Open Virtual Terminal (9600 baud)

### Test Points

| Test | Action | Expected Result |
|------|--------|-----------------|
| Water Present | Logic State HIGH | Heater ON when cold |
| Low Water | Logic State LOW | Heater OFF (safety) |
| Cold Start | PT100 = 107Ω | Heater ON |
| Target Temp | PT100 = 123Ω | Heater OFF |
| Safety Shutdown | Remove water | Instant OFF |

### Serial Output Example
```
ADC: 530 | 20.0°C | Level: OK | Heater: ON
ADC: 560 | 58.1°C | Level: OK | Heater: ON
ADC: 575 | 77.2°C | Level: OK | Heater: OFF
! LOW LEVEL - Heater OFF
```

